# EAS build/submit always archives starting from the git repository root (this file's
# location), never just the subfolder you ran the command from -- see
# https://docs.expo.dev/build-reference/easignore/. Neither TrackLine (this root) nor
# SiteSpark (site-builder/) is its own separate git repo, so every eas build/submit run
# for either app uploads BOTH apps' files unless this file trims it down.
#
# IMPORTANT: once an .easignore file exists, EAS stops reading .gitignore entirely for
# archiving purposes, so every exclusion below is copied in from the .gitignore files at
# repo root, web/, and site-builder/ (nothing here is new/riskier than what git already
# keeps out of version control) -- plus one addition at the very end.

node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
npm-debug.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
*.orig.*
.DS_Store
*.log
.env
.env.local
*.tsbuildinfo
/android/
/ios/
site-builder/ios/
site-builder/android/
.metro-health-check*
firebase-debug.log
firestore-debug.log
functions/node_modules/
functions/lib/
site-builder/firebase/functions/node_modules/
site-builder/firebase/functions/lib/
.git/

# TrackLine's offline model-training scripts + ~9MB of training artifacts (Python +
# checkpoints) -- used once, by hand, to produce the small TFJS model that's actually
# bundled at assets/models/vehicle-classifier/. Never imported by either app's runtime
# code, so every build/submit in this repo (TrackLine's own included) can safely skip
# uploading it.
training/
